## Steps to Set Up an Amazon EC2 Instance

1. Open a web browser and go to **[https://aws.amazon.com](https://aws.amazon.com)**.
2. Sign in to the **AWS Management Console**.
3. Click on **Services → EC2**.
4. Click **Launch Instance**.
5. Choose an **Amazon Machine Image (AMI)** (e.g., Amazon Linux).
6. Select an **Instance Type** (e.g., t2.micro).
7. Configure instance details.
8. Add storage as required.
9. Configure security group (allow SSH/HTTP).
10. Review and click **Launch**.
11. Create or select a **key pair**.
12. Click **Launch Instance**.

